From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Park Ju Hyung <qkrwngud825@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jan 2020 00:11:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] soong: do not use compression upon creating zip(jar)
 files

A lot of zip files are created during builds for intermediate purposes
and not using compression significantly shortens build times.

Making these uncompressed allows the host OS to utilize page-cache too.

Note that this change makes the zip files under out/dist/ to also be
uncompressed files, but it won't matter much as the ota zip file's contents
are compressed on its own.

Change-Id: I6e0a96563468e84fce148e63e4658922542b6c26
Signed-off-by: Park Ju Hyung <qkrwngud825@gmail.com>
---
 cmd/zip2zip/zip2zip_test.go | 8 --------
 third_party/zip/writer.go   | 2 +-
 zip/zip.go                  | 7 ++-----
 zip/zip_test.go             | 5 -----
 4 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

